hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2681","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abdah ad-Dabbi, 'Imran ibn Musa al-Qazzaz, and Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-'Ijli — they said: Narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, who narrated from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Zayd, that Ibn 'Abbas (RA) said:\n\nI heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivering a sermon and saying:\n\n*\The trousers are for the one who does not find a lower garment (izar)"," and the two socks (khuffayn) are for the one who does not find sandals.\""*\n\nAhmad ibn al-Miqdam added: From 'Amr ibn Dinar.\n\n---\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
